Display changes without the black screen (2026-10-21).

CarPlay fixes the stream's size, codec and frame rate when a session starts; only the view areas declared then can be
switched in place (playport-view-areas.patch). Every other change renegotiates, 5-6 s on Wi-Fi and ~10 s on the
cable, and the page showed the black "waiting for iPhone" screen meanwhile. A Tesla page asked for eight in 30
minutes (2026-10-16 diagnosis): four only made the picture sharper or switched H.264/H.265 for a shape the phone
already had, as the browser proved its decoder fast or slow, and two put back another page's frame rate.

- A change that can wait (auto quality for a shape the phone already has) is kept by the box and taken up when the
  session ends by itself; a new shape, the other orientation, a failed H.265 decode and any change by hand still
  renegotiate at once and replace it. The settings show "next connection" while one waits.
- A renegotiation for a display keeps the last picture with a notice (up to 20 s awake) instead of the black screen,
  for the page that asked and for any other page (the box marks that session end as "restarting").
- Auto reads the box's display before it decides, so it no longer sends back the fps or size another page set.
- The box logs why each change came (manual, shape, quality, codec) and the areas declared.
- Up to 8 view areas instead of 4 (4 was chosen on 2026-10-14, not a protocol limit; the F50 in the XPeng had four
  landscape shapes and no room for the split screen's portrait one). The shapes are kept most recently used last and
  the most recent are declared, ordered by size, so the same shapes make the same areas from either of them.
- A change that waits for the next session still switches to the window's area now, when one is declared.
- Both orientations are declared together when that grows the stream by at most 10%: a split screen turns the car's
  window portrait and back (XPeng with fnOS beside CarPlay, 2026-10-19: 1372x1260 with 1162x1280, 2560x2160 with
  1534x1684), and every open and close of the panel renegotiated. A phone turning (1920x1080 with 1080x1920) still
  declares one orientation, as xcertplay 1836c27 has it.
- A request for the stream already declared while the phone is between sessions only notes the area: restarting the
  invitation then cut the reconnection in progress (the same display twice within 5 s, F50 2026-10-19).

